1 NOTE He was originally named Louis Philippe Marie Victor. At an early age he 
2 CONT entered the Belgian army. In 1876 Leopold organized an international 
2 CONT association to develop central Africa, and he later financed the 
2 CONT expedition (1879-84) to the Congo River led by the British-American 
2 CONT explorer Sir Henry Morton Stanley. At the Berlin Conference of 1884-85, 
2 CONT Leopold was recognized as sovereign of the Congo Free State, annexed to 
2 CONT Belgium as the Belgian Congo in 1908, and now Zaire. Leopold incurred 
2 CONT widespread criticism for his exploitation of the Congo, and, because of 
2 CONT international protests, he was forced to institute reforms. He was 
2 CONT succeeded by his nephew Albert I.
