1 NAME Helen Louisa Georgina /Ellis/
2 GIVN Helen Louisa Georgina
2 SURN Ellis
2 _MARNM Stewart
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1863
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 AUG 1934
2 PLAC 4 Dorset Square
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 Marylebone
3 CITY London
3 POST NW1 6PU
3 CTRY England
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''From [https://glasgowmuseumsartdonors.co.uk/2018/12/16/felicia-pepys-cockerell-1890-1970/ Felicia Pepys Cockerell 1890-1970 – Glasgow Museums Art Donors Group]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT James was 43 when he married Helen Louisa Georgina Ellis at the Holy Trinity Church in Pau [&Eacute;glise Saint-André de Pau, 2 Rue O' Quin, 64000 Pau, France 43.3015037, -0.3708676] on 16 April 1885. Helena was 20 years younger t
2 CONC han her husband. She was the daughter of Major Charles David Cunynghame Ellis, late of the 60th Rifles, and granddaughter of the 1st Baron Seaford of Seaford. According to the Morning Post of 20 April 1885 Helen was also the niece
2 CONC  of Colonel Arthur E Ellis, Equerry to the Prince of Wales and of the Honourable Mrs A Harding, Lady in Waiting to the Princess of Wales, thus the bride was very well connected. The best man was Prince Clermont-Tonnerre and one of
2 CONC  the six bridesmaids was also French, which shows how integrated the Stewarts were with the French population of Pau. The honeymoon was spent in Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT James and Helen appear to have spent much of their life in Pau along with their children, Felicia Stewart who was born in 1890 and John Cecil Stewart who was born in 1897 as they are nowhere to be found in the UK Census of 1891 an
2 CONC d 1901. Only in the 1911 Census does the family appear to have given up spending winters in Pau and were now living at Stonewall Park, near Edenbridge, Kent. [https://maps.nls.uk/geo/explore/#zoom=16&lat=51.16150&lon=0.14830&layer
2 CONC s=6&b=1&marker=51.161090,0.147940 Stonewall Park, Chiddingstone Hoath, Kent TN8 7DG 51.161090, 0.147940] was a 140 acre estate about 26 miles from London. They lived in a beautiful Georgian House there but also spent time in Londo
2 CONC n for “The Season”.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=vFGg7umsGHEBxHsKM4E61g&scan=1 FreeBMD - Registration of death of Helen L. G. G. Stewart in 1934]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT July to September 1934: Registration of death of Helen L. G. G. Stewart; aged 71 [born about 1863]; in Marylebone (Volume 1a, Page 492)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.ancestry.co.uk/imageviewer/collections/1904/images/31874_221758-00549 Ancestry: 1934 probate Helen Louisa Georgina Stewart]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 November 1934 probate of Helen Louisa Georgina Stewart of [https://britishlistedbuildings.co.uk/101350632-exton-house-exton The Grove, now Exton House, Shoe Lane, Exton, Hampshire 50.9849, -1.1287], Bishops Waltham, Hampshire, 
2 CONC widow, who died 6 August 1934, at [4 Dorset Square, Marylebone, London NW1 6PU 51.5231298, -0.1599693], Middlesex, probate granted at London on 14 November 1934 to Felicia Louise Marie Pepys Cockerell, single woman, and Maurice Ed
2 CONC ward Turner, solicitor. Effects £2719 16s. 2d.
