1 NAME Guy Percy /Wyndham/ CB, MVO
2 GIVN Guy Percy
2 SURN Wyndham
2 NSFX CB, MVO
2 _MARNM Wyndham
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 19 JAN 1865
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 APR 1941
1 TITL Col.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lt.Col. Guy Percy Wyndham CB MVO (19 January 1865 – 17 April 1941) was a British Army soldier.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wyndham was born on 19 January 1865 as the son of Hon. Percy Wyndham and Madeline Caroline Frances Eden Campbell.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married twice, first in 1892 to Edwina Johanna Fitzpatrick (who died in 1919), then in 1923 to Violet Leverson, daughter and biographer of writer Ada Leverson. His son with Violet Leverson is the writer and editor Francis W
2 CONC yndham.
2 CONT
2 CONT As British military attaché in St. Petersburg, Russia, in 1909 he first warned his Austrian counterpart that an Austrian General Staff officer was supplying top secret information to the Russians. This information, however, ended 
2 CONC up on the desk of Alfred Redl, head of counter-intelligence at the Evidenzbureau in Vienna, who unfortunately was the very spy being sought.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wyndham later attained the rank of Lieutenant-Colonel in the service of the 16th The Queen's Lancers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy Percy Wyndham was a member of The Souls. Works
2 CONT
2 CONT     Life and letters of George Wyndham. Guy Percy Wyndham, John William Mackail. London: Hutchinson, 1925. Two volumes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT     Lundy, Darryl. "ThePeerage.com - Person Page 8272". The Peerage.[unreliable source]
2 CONT
