2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Luigi Amedeo, Duke of the Abruzzi (January 29, 1873 - March 18, 1933) was an Italian mountaineer and explorer, member of the royal House of Savoy and cousin of the Italian King Victor Emmanuel III. He is known for his Arcti
2 CONC c explorations and for his mountaineering expeditions, particularly to Mount Saint Elias (Alaska–Yukon) and K2 (Pakistan–China). He also served as an Italian admiral during World War I.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-119471631-1-14473/luigi-amedeo-duke-of-the-abruzzi-amedeo-of-savoy-aosta-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-f30066a1e56c05270d0714170d2a3c85&mrid=e768f00e
