1 NOTE KING OF PORTUGAL 1885; K.G.; ENTITLED TO QUARTER THE ANCIENT ROYAL ARMS OF
2 CONT ENGLAND
1 NOTE Of the royal house of Braganza. In 1891 Carlos concluded a treaty with 
2 CONT Great Britain ending a long-standing dispute over the border between the 
2 CONT Portuguese colony of Mozambique and British possessions in Africa. The 
2 CONT treaty, however, was strongly opposed in Portugal. To curb the growing 
2 CONT dissent, Carlos in 1906 gave the Portuguese statesman João Franco 
2 CONT (1855-1929) virtual dictatorial powers. Franco's harsh measures, however, 
2 CONT further increased the unrest, and resulted in the assassination of the 
2 CONT king and his eldest son. A younger son succeeded Carlos as Manuel II.
