1 NAME Halvor Orin /Halvorson/
2 GIVN Halvor Orin
2 _MARNM Halvorson
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 MAR 1897
2 PLAC River Falls
2 ADDR
3 STAE Wisconsin
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 26 OCT 1975
2 ADDR
3 CITY Minneapolis
3 STAE Minnesota
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 TITL Dr.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dr. Halvorson (1897-1975) received his B.S. in Chemical Engineering (1921) and a Ch.E. degree (1922) from the University of Minnesota. He continued graduate work in Bacteriology at Minnesota, receiving the Ph.D. in
2 CONC  1928, and remaining as a member of the Bacteriology faculty until 1949, becoming Director of the Hormel Institute there in 1943. In 1949, Dr. Halvorson was appointed head of the Bacteriology Department at the University of Illino
2 CONC is, and when the School of Life Sciences opened there in 1959, he was its first Director. He retired in 1965, returning to Minnesota as a Research Professor.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Halvorson's research interests were varied, including: application of statistical methods to microbiology; chemical and sanitary engineering; immunology; chemistry of soaps and antiseptics; virology (purification of poliovirus
2 CONC ); and bacterial physiology.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Halvorson's service to ASM was extensive: he served as President of the Society of American Bacteriologists (now ASM) in 1955; was the first Chairman of the Board of Governors of the American Academy of Microbiology (1955-58);
2 CONC  and first Chairman of the American Board of Microbiology (1958-65). He also served on the Committee for Guidance in Training for Microbiology, conducting site visits and providing evaluations for the Microbiology programs at a nu
2 CONC mber of universities. He was elected to Honorary Membership, the Society's highest honor, in 1969.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Wikipedia<br/>
