1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ronald_Ian_Campbell
2 CONT
2 CONT Rt. Hon. Sir Ronald Ian Campbell was born on 7 June 1890. He was the son of Lt.-Col. Sir Guy Theophilus Campbell, 3rd Bt. and Nina Lehmann.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was educated at Eton College, Windsor, Berkshire, England. He graduated from Magdalen College, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, in 1912 with a Bachelor of Arts (B.A.) He was appointed Companion, Order of St. Mic
2 CONC hael and St. George (C.M.G.) in 1932. He was appointed Companion, Order of the Bath (C.B.) in 1937. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary to Paris between 1938 and 1939. He was awarded the Grand Officier, Ordre national de la Légion d'honneur. He held the office of Envoy Extraordinary and Ministe
2 CONC r Plenipotentiary to Belgrade between 1939 and 1941. He was appointed Knight Commander, Order of St. Michael and St. George (K.C.M.G.) in 1941.1 He held the office of Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary to Washington 
2 CONC between 1941 and 1944. He held the office of Assistant Under-Secretary of State for the Foreign Office in 1945. He held the office of Ambassador Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary to Egypt in 1946. He was appointed Knight 
2 CONC Grand Cross, Order of St. Michael and St. George (G.C.M.G.) in 1947. He was appointed Privy Counsellor (P.C.) in 1950.
