1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Major Edward Fitzgerald Campbell was born on 7 October 1893. He was the son of Lt.-Col. Sir Guy Theophilus Campbell, 3rd Bt. and Nina Lehmann. He married Enid Leyland Speed, daughter of Major Francis Elmer Speed, o
2 CONC n 8 December 1917. He and Enid Leyland Speed were divorced in 1936. He died on 1 December 1958 at age 65, without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was educated at Eton College, Windsor, Berkshire, England. He fought in the First World War, where he was wounded and mentioned in despatches. He was educated at Royal Military College, Sandhurst, Berkshire, England. He gained 
2 CONC the rank of Major in the 60th Rifles. He was awarded the Distinguished Service Order (D.S.O.) in 1918. He gained the rank of Brevet Lieutenant-Colonel. He fought in the Second World War. He held the office of Justice of the Peace 
2 CONC (J.P.) for Argyllshire in 1952. He held the office of Deputy Lieutenant (D.L.) of Argyllshire in 1958.
