2 CONT
2 CONT * January to March 1922: Registration of marriage of Frederick P. Cockerell and Stewart; in St George Hanover Square, London (Volume 1a, Page 733)
2 CONT * January to March 1922: Registration of marriage of Felicia L.M. Stewart and Cockerell; in St George Hanover Square, London (Volume 1a, Page 738)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=zY2isum%2F5idhLWioV2QOig&scan=1 FreeBMD - Registration of death of Felicia Marie L.P. Cockerell in 1970]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT April to June 1970: Registration of death of Felicia Marie L.P. Cockerell; born 4 October 1890 [aged 80]; in Wokingham (Volume 6a, Page 659)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.ancestry.co.uk/imageviewer/collections/1904/images/48589_83024005506_3486-00283 Ancestry 19701027 probate Felicia Louise Marie Cockerell The Brook House Aldermaston Berkshire d 19700610 pr London £185911]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 27 October 1970 probate of Felicia Louise Marie Cockerell of The Brook House, Aldermaston, Berkshire, who died 10 June 1970, probate granted at London on 27 October 1970. Effects £185911
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://glasgowmuseumsartdonors.co.uk/2018/12/16/felicia-pepys-cockerell-1890-1970/ Felicia Pepys Cockerell 1890-1970 – Glasgow Museums Art Donors Group]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The portrait [of Robert Grahame of Whitehill (1759-1851) Lord Provost of Glasgow] was presented to Glasgow Museums [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelvingrove_Art_Gallery_and_Museum Kelvingrove Art Gallery and Museum, Argyle Street
2 CONC , Glasgow G3 8AG 55.8685806, -4.2905056] on Wednesday, 26 November 1947 by Felicia Pepys Cockerell of [https://britishlistedbuildings.co.uk/101117324-the-brook-house-aldermaston Brook House, Aldermaston, Berkshire RG7 4LN 51.3827,
2 CONC  -1.1523]. The first question one must ask is how a lady living in Berkshire in 1947 came to possess a portrait of a former Lord Provost of Glasgow? In fact Felicia Pepys Cockerell was the great-great granddaughter of Robert Graha
2 CONC me and the portrait was probably handed down through the generations of the family....
2 CONT
2 CONT Felicia Stewart was born in London on Saturday, 4 October 1890 at [19 Carlton House Terrace, St James's, London 51.5070077, -0.1301411]. She had one brother, John Cecil Stewart, born in 1897.
2 CONT
2 CONT James and Helen Stewart appear to have spent much of their life in Pau along with their children, Felicia Stewart who was born in 1890 and John Cecil Stewart who was born in 1897 as they are nowhere to be found in the UK Census of
2 CONC  1891 and 1901. Only in the 1911 Census does the family appear to have given up spending winters in Pau and were now living at Stonewall Park, near Edenbridge, Kent. [https://maps.nls.uk/geo/explore/#zoom=16&lat=51.16150&lon=0.148
2 CONC 30&layers=6&b=1&marker=51.161090,0.147940 Stonewall Park, Chiddingstone Hoath, Kent TN8 7DG 51.161090, 0.147940] was a 140 acre estate about 26 miles from London. They lived in a beautiful Georgian House there but also spent time 
2 CONC in London for “The Season”.
