2 CONT
2 CONT James and Helen Stewart appear to have spent much of their life in Pau along with their children, Felicia Stewart who was born in 1890 and John Cecil Stewart who was born in 1897 as they are nowhere to be found in the UK Census of
2 CONC  1891 and 1901. Only in the 1911 Census does the family appear to have given up spending winters in Pau and were now living at Stonewall Park, near Edenbridge, Kent. [https://maps.nls.uk/geo/explore/#zoom=16&lat=51.16150&lon=0.148
2 CONC 30&layers=6&b=1&marker=51.161090,0.147940 Stonewall Park, Chiddingstone Hoath, Kent TN8 7DG 51.161090, 0.147940] was a 140 acre estate about 26 miles from London. They lived in a beautiful Georgian House there but also spent time 
2 CONC in London for “The Season”.
2 CONT
2 CONT After her father's death in 1913 Felicia Stewart, her mother and brother moved to The Grove, Exton, Hampshire. They were living there by 1914.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cecil Stewart, Felicia's brother had gone to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eton_College Eton College, Eton, Berkshire SL4 6DW 51.492, -0.608] and aged only 17 joined the army on Saturday, 15 August 1914 5th Battalion Kings R
2 CONC oyal Rifle Corps. He was promoted lieutenant on Saturday, 14 August 1915 and sent to France. He survived for just a month. He was killed at the Battle of Loos on Saturday, 25 September 1915. Thus Felicia Stewart would inherit ever
2 CONC ything after her mother's death.
