1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Edward Tennant''' 
2 CONT * Born on 1 July 1897
2 CONT * Son of Edward Tennant, who became Lord Glenconner in 1911, and Pamela Wyndham, a writer. 
2 CONT * Nicknamed ‘Bim’, 
2 CONT * Educated at Winchester College until the age of 17, when it was decided he would lodge with a family in Germany to learn the language, in preparation for the Diplomatic Service. 
2 CONT * When war broke out he found himself free of school and  immediately joined the '''Grenadier Guards'''. After a year’s training in London he went to Bovington Camp, Marlow in August 1915 where his company of signallers earned dis
2 CONC tinction. 
2 CONT * Selected to go out to France, although Brigade Orders had just been issued that no one should leave England before nineteen years of age.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was killed by a sniper during the Battle of the Somme on 22nd September, 1916.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===TENNANT, The Hon. EDWARD WYNDHAM
2 CONT
2 CONT * Rank: Lieutenant
2 CONT * Date of Death: 22/09/1916
2 CONT * Age: 19
2 CONT * Regiment/Service: Grenadier Guards 4th Bn. 
2 CONT * Grave Reference: I. B. 18. 
2 CONT * Cemetery: GUILLEMONT ROAD CEMETERY, GUILLEMONT
2 CONT * '''Additional Information:''' Son of Edward Priaux, 1st Baron Glenconner and Lady Glenconner, (now Viscountess Grey of Falloden). One of the war poets. [http://www.cwgc.org/find-war-dead/casualty/534742/TENNANT,%20The%20Hon%20ED
2 CONC WARD%20WYNDHAM CWGC]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [https://livesofthefirstworldwar.org/lifestory/4389158 LOTFWW]
