1 NOTE He was educated privately and at a college in Geneva. He was in voluntary 
2 CONT exile with his father in Switzerland from May 1945 to July 1950. Leopold's 
2 CONT return to Belgium provoked much unrest, and in August 1950 the king agreed 
2 CONT to relinquish his royal prerogatives to Crown Prince Baudouin and to 
2 CONT abdicate when Baudouin attained his majority. Leopold abdicated on July 
2 CONT 16, 1951, two months before the 21st birthday of his son, and Baudouin 
2 CONT took the oath of office the next day.
