1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Major Edward FitzGerald David Campbell was born on 18 January 1910. He was the son of Sir Guy Colin Campbell, 4th Bt. and Mary Arabella Swinnerton Kemeys-Tynte. He died on 6 May 1991 at age 81 at Neots, Huntingdon,
2 CONC  Huntingdonshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Major Edward FitzGerald David Campbell usually went by his middle name of David. He was educated at Eton College, Windsor, Berkshire, England. He was educated at St. Andrews University, St. Andrews, Fife, Scotland. He fought in th
2 CONC e Second World War. He was awarded the Military Cross (M.C.) He was awarded the Emergency Reserve Decoration (E.R.D.) He gained the rank of Major in the Black Watch. He fought in the Korean War between 1952 and 1954. He was second
2 CONC  in command of the Kenya Regiment between 1954 and 1956. He fought in the Kenyan Campaign between 1954 and 1956, against the Mau Maus.
