1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Clavell Mansel was born on 9 January 1917. He was the son of Major Rhys Clavell Mansel and Sylvia Nina Campbell. He married Damaris Joan Hyde-Thomson, daughter of Robert Hyde Hyde-Thomson and Joan Perronet Sel
2 CONC ls, on 11 August 1945. He died on 13 September 2007 at age 90 at Dorchester, Dorset, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was educated at Eton College, Windsor, Berkshire, England. He graduated from Christ Church, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, EnglandG, in 1938 with a Bachelor of Arts (B.A.). He fought in the Second World War. He gained 
2 CONC the rank of Captain in 1942 in the Rifle Brigade. He gained the rank of Major in 1946. He held the office of Justice of the Peace (J.P.) for Wareham between 1961 and 1982. He held the office of High Sheriff of Dorset in 1968. He g
2 CONC raduated from Christ Church, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, in 1968 with a Master of Arts (M.A.) He held the office of Deputy Lieutenant (D.L.) of Dorset in 1974. He lived in 2003 at The Old Parsonage, Kimmeridge
2 CONC , Dorset, England.
