1 NAME Pauline Laetitia /Tennant/
2 GIVN Pauline Laetitia
2 SURN Tennant
2 _MARNM Tennant
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 6 FEB 1929
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 DEC 2008
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pauline_Tennant
2 CONT
2 CONT Pauline Laetitia Tennant, later Pauline Graham, Pauline Rumbold or Lady Rumbold (6 February 1927 – 6 December 2008) was an English actress, poet and socialite.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Born into an aristocratic family, she was the daughter of David Pax Tennant and Hermione Baddeley. She was married three times, to Julian Pitt-Rivers (1946–53); Euan Douglas Graham, grandson of the fifth Duke of Montrose (from 195
2 CONC 4); and then Sir Anthony Rumbold (1974–83).
2 CONT
2 CONT Stage and screen
2 CONT
2 CONT Tennant played on the West End stage in Ben Travers' She Followed Me About (1943) and alongside Fay Compton in No Medals (1947). She also appeared in two films: Great Day (1945, screen debut) and The Queen of Spades (1949).
2 CONT
2 CONT In an obituary for The Independent, the writer Philip Hoare described Tennant as "a true bohemian aristocrat – a tension of qualities that were literally in her genes." During her younger years she was often seen at the bar of the
2 CONC  prestigious Ritz, London
