1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles W. Burns, 86, of Harford, entered into rest on April 20, 2016. He is survived by his loving wife of almost 25 years, Lenore.
2 CONT Charles is also survived by his children, Georgia Conover, Alex and Mae Burns, Carolyn Dunback, Chris and Rebecca Penny, and Richard and Barbara Penny; many grandchildren and great grandchildren; three sisters; five brothers; and 
2 CONC numerous nieces and nephews. 
2 CONT He was predeceased by two sons, Claude Burns and Burt Whittemore.
2 CONT Charles was employed as a truck driver with Reich Trucking until they closed and then with Endless Mountains Stone. He served with the United States Army during Korea. 
2 CONT Charles had the ability to fix anything. He was always busy doing something. He took extremely good care of his yard and home. 
2 CONT Charles also helped anyone he found with a need and everyone he met loved him. 
2 CONT Interment was made in New Milford Cemetery at on Saturday, April 23, 2016. At Charles' request, there were no calling hours. 
2 CONT Arrangements are under the direction of the Tuttle-Yeisley Funeral Home, Inc., Hallstead.
2 CONT Published in Susquehanna County Independent from Apr. 28, 2016* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/161829702/charles-w-burns Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 26
