2 CONT
2 CONT Dwight P. Babcock
2 CONT
2 CONT PHELPS — Dwight P. Babcock, 63, of Park Street, Phelps, passed away Saturday (Feb. 2, 2008) at home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call from 2 to 4 p.m. and 7 to 9 p.m. Tuesday (Feb. 5) at the Patrick Funeral Home, 26 W. Main St., Clifton Springs. Funeral services will be held at 11 a.m. Wednesday (Feb. 6) at the funeral home with the Rev. Lynn Sp
2 CONC ence officiating.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial will be at the convenience of the family in St. Agnes Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may contribute to their favorite charity in Dwight's memory.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dwight was born Dec. 19, 1944, in Afton, Chenango County, the son of Wallace and Edna Babcock. He served his country in the Army from 1966 to 1969. Dwight was employed by Great Lakes Kraut in Shortsville. Dwight was a workaholic a
2 CONC nd family man rolled into one. "A Father carries pictures where his money used to be." This saying sums up Dwight Babcock. He was a loving father and grandfather and will be sadly missed by all of his loving friends and family.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his children, Katrina Babcock, Phillip Babcock and Kyle Babcock, all of Phelps; wife, Jean Babcock, of Phelps; grandchildren, Makayla and Madison; brothers, Wallace (Carolyn) Babcock of Texas, Leo (Candice) Babco
2 CONC ck of Fla., Gary (Lois) Babcock of Bainbridge, Chenango
2 CONT County and Everett (Jo) Babcock of Ovid; sisters, Lucille (Robert) Sherpinskas of N.C., Clara (Herman) Diagostino of Miss., and Mary (Ernest) Franklin of Mount Upton, Chenango County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dwight was predeceased by his brother, Thomas Babcock, and sister, Sharon Church.
