1 NAME Riccardo /Paternò di Montecupo/
2 GIVN Riccardo
2 _MARNM Paternò di Montecupo
2 NICK Riccard Paternò principe di Cerenzia
1 NAME Riccardo Paternò di Montecupo
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 5 OCT 1945
2 ADDR
3 CITY Naples
3 STAE Campania
3 CTRY Italy
1 OCCU
1 TITL Prince
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Grand Chancellor of the Order of Malta
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.orderofmalta.int/government/grand-chancellor/
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Naples on 5 October 1945, he graduated in Law at the Naples University Federico II. Riccardo Paternò di Montecupo is a widower and father of three.
2 CONT
2 CONT He has taught International Economics at several Italian universities and as Visiting Professor at the London School of Economics. He held the chair of International Economics at the Faculty of Economics at the University of Naple
2 CONC s for 35 years. He has numerous publications to his credit and is the author of several books on international economics.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1983 to 1994, he was an economic advisor to several Ministers of the Italian Republic (Industry, Defence) as well as to the Prime Minister’s Office. He was also a member of the Technical Scientific Committee for Economic Plan
2 CONC ning, an economic advisor to Confindustria and numerous Italian and foreign companies. He was a member of the Scientific Committee of the Foreign Trade Institute and is a member of the Italian Society of Economists. He has written
2 CONC  numerous editorials for the daily newspaper ‘Il Mattino’ in Naples.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is president of the Ernst&Young Foundation, whose aim is to give opportunities to young people in disadvantaged situations. He is the promoter of a Unitalsi structure in Naples, ‘Casa Sveva’, to accommodate families of children
2 CONC  hospitalised at paediatric centres in Campania. Since 1962, he has served as a UNITALSI volunteer in pilgrimages to the Shrines of Lourdes and Loreto. He founded and chairs the ‘Renato and Laura Paternò’ Foundation, with charitab
2 CONC le aims.
2 CONT
2 CONT He joined the Order of Malta in 1979 and has been at the head of the Association of Italian Knights since 2016. As president of the Italian Association, he is also head of the Military Corps, which has been run for over a century 
2 CONC in close cooperation between the Italian Army and the Order of Malta, specialised in military healthcare. He has participated in numerous international pilgrimages to the Sanctuary of Lourdes and national pilgrimages to Assisi and
2 CONC  Loreto. He served as Deputy Observer of the Order of Malta’s mission to the Food and Agriculture Organisation of the United Nations (FAO).
2 CONT
2 CONT He took office as Grand Chancellor on 3 September 2022. The Extraordinary Chapter General of 25-29 January 2023 has reconfirmed him for another six years.
